  "description": "VAVHEI crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: 5(C5 H6 N1 1+),C28 H6 F42 Lu5 O34 5-,5(C5 H5 N1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Lu1 (Lu) has 8 O neighbors; Lu2 (Lu) has 8 O neighbors; Lu3 (Lu) has 8 O neighbors; Lu4 (Lu) has 8 O neighbors; Lu5 (Lu) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.638-3.743 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.34-109.71°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C58H40F42Lu5N6O35.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
